// Analyzed file list for tasks/serv_rvfi_insn_sll.
//
// Paths are relative to the PACKAGE ROOT: the drivers `cd $task_root` before
// sourcing lists/tc_elab.tcl, and `taskdefs.slang_args` runs slang from the
// same place, so one spelling serves both.
//
// Two consumers read this one list:
//   * lists/tc_elab.tcl:  analyze -sv12 -f lists/tc_elab.files
//   * taskdefs.slang_args, which filters it into tc_elab.files.slang for the
//     design map.
// v5/round.py appends one `../submission/<worker>.sv` line per worker at the
// END, so the file must end with a newline and must not close with a `-y` or
// other non-source directive -- an appended source line has to stay a source
// line.
//
// ORDER MATTERS, and this is the whole subtlety of the SERV packages.
// `ft/defines.sv` is a HEADER, not a module, and it is listed first on
// purpose. The source flow (engine/ric3.toml) names it under `include_files`;
// here it is the first analyzed file so that its `RISCV_FORMAL` and the
// `rvfi_macros.vh` it pulls in are defined before anything else compiles.
// The SERV RTL does NOT include it -- serv_top.v:25, serv_rf_top.v:46 and
// serv_debug.v:16 guard the whole rvfi port list behind `ifdef RISCV_FORMAL,
// so with the header anywhere later the core would elaborate WITHOUT its rvfi
// outputs and ft/wrapper.sv's `RVFI_CONN would name ports that do not exist.
// It carries its own `ifndef DEFINES_SV guard, so the `include "defines.sv"
// that sva/ and ft/ each do is then inert.

+incdir+ft

// --- riscv-formal configuration header, first: see above --------------------
ft/defines.sv

// --- SERV RISC-V core, byte-identical upstream RTL --------------------------
rtl/serv_bufreg.v
rtl/serv_bufreg2.v
rtl/serv_alu.v
rtl/serv_csr.v
rtl/serv_ctrl.v
rtl/serv_decode.v
rtl/serv_immdec.v
rtl/serv_mem_if.v
rtl/serv_rf_if.v
rtl/serv_rf_ram.v
rtl/serv_rf_ram_if.v
rtl/serv_state.v
rtl/serv_debug.v
rtl/serv_top.v
rtl/serv_rf_top.v

// --- the riscv-formal instruction model and the check that reads it ---------
sva/insn_sll.v
sva/rvfi_insn_check.sv

// --- the rvfi wrapper around the core, and the formal top -------------------
ft/wrapper.sv
ft/tb.sv

// --- phase-1 candidate targets. LAST, because the bind at the
// --- end of the file must be analyzed after `testbench` exists.
sva/targets_serv_rvfi_insn_sll.sv
